#CrashLoopBackoff

What is CrashLoopBackOff❓ 

Kubernetes "CrashLoopBackOff" is a state when a container inside a pod fails to start up and keeps crashing repeatedly. It defines that something is wrong with your container or application you are trying to run inside the pod.

If the Kubernetes fails in the first attempt to start up the container, it will keep retrying ♻️ the same step with an increasing 📈 back-off delay. This is what the "BackOff" represents in "CrashLoopBackOff".

Some factors that can get a Pod into a CrashLoopBackOff state: 
✒️ Misconfiguration i.e. incorrect details or details not provided in configuration files.
✒️ It may be due to insufficient 🫗 resources i.e. Memory or CPU
✒️ There may be chances the liveness probes are not configured correctly, like incorrect paths, endpoints, etc.
✒️ It may be due to an error or bug 🐞 in application code.
✒️ Wrong Command Line Arguments.

Resolution: 🤔 
Run the following commands to catch the issue:💡 
🔸kubectl describe pod <pod_name>
🔸kubectl logs <pod_name> ▶️ to fetch the logs 
🔸kubectl logs <pod_name> -c <container_name>▶️ to fetch log at container level
🔸kubectl get events▶️ to look at events before the pod crashed

